; SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
; count's result compares as an unsigned number: (< (count [1 2]) -9) is true, (> (count []) -1)
; false, (max (count [1 2]) -9) is -9, and a loop counting from a count up to a negative bound
; never ends. count is inlined as jank.runtime.sequence_length (usize) and < as jank.runtime.lt,
; whose two-primitive overload is C++'s l < r: the negative i64 converts to a huge unsigned value.
; Through a call (identity, a fn) count is boxed and compares right.
; Its last line never ends: run it in a terminal, or with stdbuf -o0 when piped (jank buffers a
; pipe's output, and flush is not ported), to see the lines before it.
(println "passing (count boxed by a call):" (< (identity (count [1 2])) -9) "expected false")
(println "expected false:" (< (count [1 2]) -9))
(println "expected true: " (> (count []) -1))
(println "expected 2:    " (max (count [1 2]) -9))
(println "expected true: " (let [n (count "ab")] (> n -1)))
(println "a loop from a count to a negative bound (expected 2, never ends):")
(println (loop [a (count "ab")] (if (< a -9) (recur (+ a 1)) a)))
